<section>
    <div class="container-narrow">
        <h1>Install ProVerif</h1>
        <p class="subtitle">
            ProVerif is Free Software distributed under <a
                href="LICENSE">GPLv2</a>.
        </p>

        <div class="shadow-sm p-4 border mt-5">
            <p>
                Install with <a href="https://opam.ocaml.org/">OPAM</a>
            </p>
            <pre class="code">opam install proverif</pre>
        </div>

        <p class="mt-4">
            There might also be a dedicated package for proverif in your package manager.
            If you want to instead install it manually, consult the <a href="README">README</a> and download:
        </p>

        <ul>
            <li>the source package <a href="proverifVERSION.tar.gz">ProVerif version VERSION source</a> (gzipped tar file) or
                the binary package <a href="proverifbinVERSION.tar.gz">ProVerif version VERSION, for Windows</a></li>
            <li>and the documentation package <a href="proverifdocVERSION.tar.gz">ProVerif version VERSION, documentation</a>.
            </li>
        </ul>

        <p class="mt-4">

            More options on how to install ProVerif can be found in the
            <a href="https://bblanche.gitlabpages.inria.fr/proverif/manual.pdf">manual</a>.
        </p>
    </div>
</section>

<hr/>

<section>
    <div class="container-narrow">
        <h2 class="mt-0">Editor Support</h2>
        <div class="row">
            <div class="col-md-6">
                <p>
                    ProVerif has first-class editor support in VSCode with a language server.
                    Install the <a href="https://marketplace.visualstudio.com/items?itemName=ProVerif.vscode-proverif">ProVerif
                    Language Server</a>.
                </p>

                <p class="mt-3">
                    Further, there is
                </p>
                <ul>
                    <li>
                        a <a href="https://github.com/lifepillar/vim-formal-package">Vim mode</a> with
                        support for ProVerif,
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        for emacs, there is proverif.el provided in the ProVerif distribution
                        (see the <a href="https://bblanche.gitlabpages.inria.fr/proverif/manual.pdf">manual</a>),
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        an <a href="https://paolo.science/anbx/ide/">Eclipse plug-in</a> by Rémi Garcia and Paolo
                        Modesti.
                    </li>
                </ul>
            </div>
            <div class="col-md-6">
                <img src="images/vscode-extension.png" class="img-fluid shadow" alt="VSCode Extension">
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>


<script src="./js/bootstrap.bundle.min.js"></script>
